WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:04.237
-My first guest is the host of
"Late Night with Seth Meyers,"

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:07.673
which airs weeknights on NBC
right after our show

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:09.575
and is also available
on Peacock.

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:13.613
Please welcome Seth Meyers,
ladies and gentlemen!

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:17.416
-♪ Seth Adam Meyers
wasn't hard to book ♪

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:21.454
♪ If you don't know the reason,
you need to take a closer look ♪

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:25.758
♪ If you know Seth Meyers
and can't get enough ♪

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:29.929
♪ Stay on this channel,
he's on right after us ♪

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:30.996
♪ Yeah ♪

00:00:30.996 --> 00:00:33.032
-Oh!

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:35.168
-That's got to feel great, huh?

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:37.136
-It's nice -- You know,
we haven't done it yet.

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:39.338
So to be in front of an audience
again, my goodness.

00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:40.706
-It's unbelievable.
Yeah, they're the best.

00:00:40.706 --> 00:00:42.875
Thank you guys.
-Yeah, real, live

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:45.111
[ Cheers and applause ]
Real, live human beings.

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.545
-Yeah, I --

00:00:46.545 --> 00:00:49.848
Thank you for coming down
and doing the show with us.

00:00:49.848 --> 00:00:50.984
I know --
-You make it very easy.

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:51.985
It's two floors.

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.119
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.721
-The family's good?
Alexi's good?

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.022
-Yeah, the kids are great.
-Yeah.

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:59.024
-I mean, they're great. Right?

00:00:59.024 --> 00:01:00.059
-Yeah.
-No, I just want

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:02.461
to establish that
before I keep going.

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:03.930
-Yeah, of course.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.098
-I don't --

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:07.066
You know, I like my time
with them to be positive.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:11.270
But I would like this time now
to sort of air some grievances.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:13.172
-Oh, really?
-Just minor things.

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:14.741
-Sure.
-'Cause I don't --

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:18.344
I feel like they watch late-
night TV, so they'll see this,

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.579
and it's just easier for me
if they hear it this way.

00:01:20.579 --> 00:01:22.515
-No, of course, of course.
So smart. Yes.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:24.317
-So, they --
I have two beautiful boys.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.385
-Yeah, I know, I love them.

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:28.888
-Their smiles light up a room.
-Yeah.

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:33.059
-The most natural, angelic,
cherubic smiles.

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:35.394
-Yes.
-You take out a camera --

00:01:35.394 --> 00:01:37.830
Crazy rictus grins.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:40.699
It's like --

00:01:40.699 --> 00:01:43.169
We have no good photos
of them smiling,

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.837
'cause they're like
laughing and being real,

00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:47.540
and then it's like
they got bit by a scorpion.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.540
And they're like --

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:49.875
-Dude, that is weird.

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:51.110
Why do --
-It's awful.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.879
-My kids do that, too.
-And I show it to them

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:55.315
on the phone, I'm like, "I can't
let people look at this.

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:56.382
You understand?"

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.217
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.217 --> 00:01:59.618
-You're too cute for this.

00:01:59.618 --> 00:02:01.587
-"You're too cute --
You're better than this, guys."

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:03.756
-Yes! That's it. But they're
learning how to smile.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.658
-They're learning -- It's so
weird that they don't --

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.893
Yeah, they just hate --
-We've learned over the years,

00:02:07.893 --> 00:02:09.228
you go like, "Smile for a
picture."

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:11.830
-Yeah, I show like, I show them
adults on Instagram.

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:13.866
I'm like, "None of these people
are really happy.

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:15.735
They've just learned --

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.270
They've learned to fake it.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.605
-Yes!
-Come on, guys!

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:20.272
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.272 --> 00:02:21.741
-Awful.
-Awful, well, yeah.

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:23.075
-I hope you're watching.

00:02:23.075 --> 00:02:24.744
-They're the cutest kids
in the world.

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.612
-They're two good dudes.

00:02:26.612 --> 00:02:28.847
-You're doing stand-up
shows again.

00:02:28.847 --> 00:02:30.750
-Yeah. I've done a couple.
It's really nice.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.719
People are so happy
to just be out.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:34.153
-Yeah, how does it feel
to perform?

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:38.423
-It's great. I did stand-up
in a tent in a parking lot,

00:02:38.423 --> 00:02:39.892
and it was wonderful.

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:44.230
And I think that speaks to how
lousy the last year has been.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.831
-Yeah.
-That you feel like

00:02:45.831 --> 00:02:47.199
you're walking into
a night club,

00:02:47.199 --> 00:02:50.336
when you're like, "Look at this.
A tent in a parking lot!"

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.538
-"Look at that!"
-"Oh!

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:54.473
Top of the world!"

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:55.742
-"You did this for me!"

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:58.144
-Yeah, but it's really fun.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:01.881
And I think these
next few years, I think

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:04.350
live performance, live music,
people are just going to be --

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.485
Sports. Everybody's going to be
happy to be in the same place,

00:03:06.485 --> 00:03:07.754
which is cool.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:11.157
-Yeah, I know you're doing
a gig in Boston soon.

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:12.858
-Yes. Yeah, July.

00:03:12.858 --> 00:03:14.494
-Where are you playing?
-The Wilbur? You know the --

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:15.662
The best, right?

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:18.130
-I think I recorded
a comedy thing there.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.365
-Yeah, you did.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.233
-It's one of the best theaters
in the country.

00:03:21.233 --> 00:03:22.702
-So I'm looking forward to that.
And of course --

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:24.203
-I mean, you're Boston,
I mean, you're --

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:26.104
-I'm, you know, Southern
New Hampshire, which we count --

00:03:26.104 --> 00:03:28.641
We say is Boston, and Boston
says, "No, you're not."

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:29.909
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.477
-But that's Boston.
-That's Boston, right.

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:35.915
-But I know -- I think you are
the biggest Red Sox fan.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.583
-I had a run there where I think

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:39.719
no one cared more
about the Red Sox than I did.

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.120
-Maybe Mike Schur.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.623
-Mike Schur, our dear friend
who worked at "SNL" with us

00:03:44.623 --> 00:03:46.292
and then went on to --

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.360
Nothing. To just fail.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.496
-No, he did "The Office."

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.965
-"The Office," "Parks and Rec,"
"The Good Place."

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:54.233
-He's one of our friends.

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:55.535
-He does an incredible job,
yeah.

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:57.169
-Yeah, he's brilliant.
But do you remember

00:03:57.169 --> 00:03:59.204
when we went out drinking
one night with David Wells?

00:03:59.204 --> 00:04:01.874
-Yeah. I mean,
you guys know David Wells.

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:04.010
-One of the best pitchers
in the history of baseball.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:08.314
-And one of the greatest
partiers of all time.

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:10.516
-He's a Yankee, New York --
He's a legend.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:12.785
And he was so much fun.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.353
We used to hang out with him
whenever we got a chance.

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:15.854
-Yep.
-And then we went out,

00:04:15.854 --> 00:04:18.957
I go, "Seth, let's just do it.
Wellsie's around. Let's do it."

00:04:18.957 --> 00:04:20.827
-And we had an incredible night
with David Wells.

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:22.995
-He's unbelievable, though.
-He's unbelievable.

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:25.298
The thing about him is, and I
don't know if you found this.

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:27.700
I felt like when you went out
and drank with David Wells,

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.303
he would tell you
all the secrets of baseball.

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:32.438
Like, it felt like
he was giving you

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:34.707
all the mysteries of the sport.
-Yeah.

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:37.677
-And yet with each mystery,
he'd also make do you a shot.

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:39.111
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:40.480
And so the next morning,
you'd wake up,

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.948
and it was all gone.
-Couldn't remember anything.

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:43.582
-You couldn't remember
any of it.

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:44.884
That's how he gets you.

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:46.585
-Yeah, because I do remember him
having great stories,

00:04:46.585 --> 00:04:48.354
but right off
the top of my head,

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:49.889
I don't remember
any of the great stories.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:52.358
But he's such a good hang.
But we went out --

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:55.928
-We went out, and I made the
mistake of texting Mike Schur,

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:58.731
who's another dyed-in-the-wool
Red Sox fan.

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:02.734
And he was so upset to hear
that I was out with a Yankee.

00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:04.671
And this is before the Red Sox
won the World Series.

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:07.974
So we were a little bit
more irrational.

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:09.341
And I came in the next day,

00:05:09.341 --> 00:05:11.243
and he had gone to
the New York Yankees store,

00:05:11.243 --> 00:05:14.046
which is right around here
where they just sell merch.

00:05:14.046 --> 00:05:15.281
-That's right.
-And he had --

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:17.583
This is the way he burned me.

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:22.588
He spent $500 on Yankees stuff
and filled my office.

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:24.624
-I mean, the ceiling,
everything.

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:25.824
-Pillows.

00:05:25.824 --> 00:05:28.094
There was a Yankee lamp.

00:05:28.094 --> 00:05:29.962
-No, the best move was,
do you remember,

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:31.263
your screen saver was Yankees.

00:05:31.263 --> 00:05:32.598
-Yeah, screen saver.

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:33.732
A Yankee mouse pad.

00:05:33.732 --> 00:05:35.334
-No, he took it
to the next level.

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:38.237
He's like, "Oh, Mr. Yankee.
Come on in.

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:39.605
You love the Yankees so much.

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:41.908
You go out drinking with them.
Why don't you come in?"

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:43.910
-He was like,
"I thought you'd enjoy --

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:47.813
Consider this a parting gift,
as you are now dead to me."

00:05:47.813 --> 00:05:49.882
-I think on the front
of the door was either Wells

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.651
or somebody, or Jeter,
or somebody.

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:53.018
-It was --
He did not react well.

00:05:53.018 --> 00:05:54.554
We got over it. We got over it.

00:05:54.554 --> 00:05:55.754
-Dude, congrats on "Late Night."

00:05:55.754 --> 00:05:56.956
How many years has it been now,
seven years?

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:58.090
-Seven. Isn't that nuts?

00:05:58.090 --> 00:05:59.825
I mean, yeah.
-Ah, I'm so happy.

00:05:59.825 --> 00:06:01.193
-Seven years.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:01.193 --> 00:06:03.261
-You're kicking butt.

00:06:03.261 --> 00:06:04.863
The show's fantastic.

00:06:04.863 --> 00:06:06.065
You're as sharp as ever.

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:07.233
The writing is awesome.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:09.068
-Those guys do
an amazing job, yeah.

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:10.269
-Are you loving it?

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:12.138
-Yeah! I mean, I can't believe,

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:13.973
you know, especially
this last year.

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:16.542
I've always felt incredibly
grateful to have a show.

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:18.110
But this last year
has been insane

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.112
to be able to still
go and do your job

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:21.747
even though this year
has been such a drag.

00:06:21.747 --> 00:06:23.582
And so I felt --
-Thank you for doing it.

00:06:23.582 --> 00:06:25.551
We all needed it.
-Thank you, buddy.

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:27.119
-I mean, everyone needed it,
and so, yeah.

00:06:27.119 --> 00:06:29.155
Just for you being there
and showing up was one thing,

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:31.924
but then doing great comedy and
good work, we're like, "Yes!

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:33.392
Thank you.
Just get us through this."

00:06:33.392 --> 00:06:35.495
-Well, it was an honor

00:06:35.495 --> 00:06:37.796
to just be a part
of all the late night shows.

00:06:37.796 --> 00:06:40.266
We're getting it done.
-We love you, bud. I'm so happy.

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:41.467
-Thank you.
-Thanks for coming on the show.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:42.968
Seth Meyers.

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:46.838
You can catch "Late Night with
Seth Meyers" on NBC and Peacock

00:06:46.838 --> 00:06:48.540
right after our show.
Just don't change the channel.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:49.575
-Yeah.
-You'll see more of Seth.

